<svg width="760" height="950" viewBox="0 0 760 950" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">

<style>
.box { fill: #1f2937; stroke: #6366f1; stroke-width: 1.5; rx: 10; }
.title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: bold; fill: #ffffff; text-anchor: middle; }
.text { font-size: 12px; fill: #e5e7eb; text-anchor: middle; }
.small { font-size: 11px; fill: #9ca3af; text-anchor: middle; }

.arrow { stroke: #6b7280; stroke-width: 1.3; marker-end: url(#arrow); }
.main { fill: #111827; font-size: 17px; font-weight: bold; text-anchor: middle; }
</style>

<defs>
  <marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="8" refY="3" orient="auto">
    <polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#6b7280"/>
  </marker>
</defs>

<!-- Title -->
<text x="380" y="40" class="main">Bad Debt Prediction – End-to-End Flow</text>

<!-- 1 -->
<rect x="100" y="80" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="110" class="title">1. Data Preprocessing & EDA</text>
<text x="380" y="135" class="text">Missing values • duplicates • outliers handling</text>
<text x="380" y="155" class="text">EDA: repayment behaviour, delinquency, correlations</text>
<text x="380" y="175" class="small">Key drivers: credit score, repayment history, delinquency</text>

<line x1="380" y1="185" x2="380" y2="225" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 2 -->
<rect x="100" y="225" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="255" class="title">2. Feature Engineering</text>
<text x="380" y="280" class="text">CR21 vs CR22 → selected CR22 for better separation</text>
<text x="380" y="300" class="text">WoE binning • IV-based feature selection</text>
<text x="380" y="320" class="small">Transforms features into risk-aligned, interpretable variables</text>

<line x1="380" y1="330" x2="380" y2="370" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 3 -->
<rect x="100" y="370" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="400" class="title">3. Class Imbalance Handling</text>
<text x="380" y="425" class="text">Under-sampling tested → information loss</text>
<text x="380" y="445" class="text">SMOTE-Tomek: synthetic samples + boundary cleaning</text>
<text x="380" y="465" class="small">Improves recall of bad customers (critical business metric)</text>

<line x1="380" y1="475" x2="380" y2="515" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 4 -->
<rect x="100" y="515" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="545" class="title">4. Model Selection</text>
<text x="380" y="570" class="text">Models: Logistic Regression • Random Forest • XGBoost • CatBoost</text>
<text x="380" y="590" class="text">Evaluated on generalisation & recall performance</text>
<text x="380" y="610" class="small">Selected: Random Forest (best recall + stability balance)</text>

<line x1="380" y1="620" x2="380" y2="660" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 5 -->
<rect x="100" y="660" width="560" height="110" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="690" class="title">5. Model Evaluation</text>
<text x="380" y="715" class="text">ROC-AUC: 0.74 • Gini: 0.48 • KS: 34%</text>
<text x="380" y="735" class="text">Recall (Bad): 60% → identifies majority of defaulters</text>
<text x="380" y="755" class="small">Optimised for high recall to minimize financial loss</text>

<line x1="380" y1="770" x2="380" y2="810" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 6 -->
<rect x="100" y="810" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="840" class="title">6. Performance Analysis</text>
<text x="380" y="865" class="text">Confusion Matrix • ROC Curve • Gini Curve</text>
<text x="380" y="885" class="text">Feature Importance → key risk drivers</text>

<line x1="380" y1="900" x2="380" y2="940" class="arrow"/>

<!-- 7 -->
<rect x="100" y="940" width="560" height="100" class="box"/>
<text x="380" y="970" class="title">7. PSI & CSI Monitoring</text>
<text x="380" y="995" class="text">PSI: 0.39 → significant data drift</text>
<text x="380" y="1015" class="text">CSI: stable → feature importance unchanged</text>
<text x="380" y="1035" class="small">Concept drift → monitoring, WoE recalibration, retraining</text>

</svg>
